hk: don't compress input attachments

On G14S (M2 Pro) a compressed RGBA16F input attachment, read in a subpass
that writes a linear RGB10A2 colour attachment, comes back wrong along the
image edges. wlroots' two-pass Vulkan renderer does exactly that for 10-bit
scanout, and every new frame flickers a border round the panel; the same
pass writing linear BGRA8 is fine. Leaving the blend image uncompressed
(HK_NOCOMPRESS=input in a debug build) fixes it, as ASAHI_MESA_DEBUG=nocompress
does, so treat input attachments like feedback loops.

--- a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_image.c
+++ b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_image.c
@@ -239,18 +239,25 @@
     * Feedback loops are problematic with compression. The GL driver bans them.
     * Interestingly, the relevant CTS tests pass on G13G and G14C, but not on
     * G13D. For now, conservatively ban compression with feedback loops.
+    *
+    * Input attachments go the same way: on G14S, a compressed RGBA16F input
+    * attachment read in a subpass that writes a linear RGB10A2 colour
+    * attachment comes back wrong along the image edges, which wlroots'
+    * two-pass Vulkan renderer hits on every frame of 10-bit scanout.
     */
    if (usage &
        (VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT | VK_IMAGE_USAGE_STORAGE_BIT |
-        VK_IMAGE_USAGE_ATTACHMENT_FEEDBACK_LOOP_BIT_EXT)) {
+        VK_IMAGE_USAGE_ATTACHMENT_FEEDBACK_LOOP_BIT_EXT |
+        VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT)) {
 
       perf_debug_dev(
-         dev, "No compression: incompatible usage -%s%s%s",
+         dev, "No compression: incompatible usage -%s%s%s%s",
          (usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT) ? " host-transfer" : "",
          (usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_STORAGE_BIT) ? " storage" : "",
          (usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_ATTACHMENT_FEEDBACK_LOOP_BIT_EXT)
             ? " feedback-loop"
-            : "");
+            : "",
+         (usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT) ? " input-attachment" : "");
       return false;
    }
 
